 al. 1996, Gueth-Hallonet et al.1998, Harborth et al.1999) apparently as a result of dimerization of the NuMA rod domains followed by association of multiple NuMA dimers through their tail domains.", "literatureReference": [380471, {"dbId": 380472, "displayName": "Self assembly of NuMA: multiarm oligomers as structural units of a nuclear lattice", "title": "Self assembly of NuMA: multiarm oligomers as structural units of a nuclear lattice", "journal": "EMBO J", "pages": "1689-700", "pubMedIdentifier": 10075938, "volume": 18, "year": 1999, "url": "http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/10075938", "className": "LiteratureReference", "schemaClass": "LiteratureReference"}, {"dbId": 380494, "displayName": "NuMA assembles into an extensive filamentous structure when expressed in the cell cytoplasm", "title": "NuMA assembles into an extensive filamentous structure when expressed in the cell cytoplasm", "journal": "J Cell Sci", "pages": "619-30", "pubMedIdentifier": 8907707, "volume": 109, "year": 1996, "url": "http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/8907707", "className": "LiteratureReference", "schemaClass": "LiteratureReference"}, {"dbId": 380480, "displayName": "Induction of a regular nuclear lattice by overexpression of NuMA", "title": "Induction of a regular nuclear lattice by overexpression of NuMA", "journal": "Exp Cell Res", "pages": "434-52", "pubMedIdentifier": 9743603, "volume": 243, "year": 1998, "url": "http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/9743603", "className": "LiteratureReference", "schemaClass": "LiteratureReference"}], "className": "Summation", "schemaClass": "Summation"}], "reviewStatus": {"dbId": 9821382, "displayName": "five stars", "definition": "externally reviewed", "name": ["five stars"], "className": "ReviewStatus", "schemaClass": "ReviewStatus"}, "updateTrackers": [{"dbId": 9781086, "displayName": "Update Tracker - [Reaction:380316] Association of NuMA with microtubules - v61:[add_removeInput, modifyText]", "action": ["add_removeInput", "modifyText"], "upda